  "_readme": [
    "ES->EN AUTO PARTS GLOSSARY — shared infrastructure, not a search hack.",
    "",
    "Purpose: the canonical Spanish-to-English mapping for auto-part names,",
    "maintained once and consumed by every surface that needs it:",
    "  1. Aria Auto search (browser) — inlined into index.html by running",
    "     `node scripts/build-parts-glossary-inline.mjs` (see the GENERATED",
    "     notice above AUTO_PART_TERMS_ES_EN in index.html).",
    "  2. The future Aria AI assistant — imports THIS JSON file directly",
    "     (Node: JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(...))) for part-name translation",
    "     and recognition. Nothing about this file's structure is",
    "     search-specific, so the assistant can adopt it as-is.",
    "",
    "DO NOT rebuild this as a duplicate list elsewhere. If a new consumer",
    "needs part-name knowledge, it imports this file.",
    "",
    "Versioning (semver):",
    "  patch — new synonyms or typo fixes, no new concepts;",
    "  minor — new part concepts added;",
    "  major — schema change (entry shape, category list).",
    "",
    "Entry shape:",
    "  es           canonical Spanish term (lowercase, with accents)",
    "  en           English term(s); the search uses en[0]",
    "  category     one of: brakes, filters, fluids, ignition, electrical,",
    "               lighting, cooling, fuel, exhaust, belts, suspension,",
    "               steering, drivetrain, transmission, wipers, body,",
    "               wheels, sensors",
    "  synonyms_es  other Spanish spellings/variants, incl. singular/plural",
    "               and regionalisms (e.g. Peruvian 'faja' for belt)",
    "  notes        optional translator note",
    "",
    "Matching rules live with the consumer (accent- and case-insensitive,",
    "whole-word, longest-phrase-first); this file holds only knowledge."
  ],
